@startuml
' claim: nothing is published unless two separate runners produced the same bytes
participant "release.yml (caller)" as C
participant "quality.yml" as Q
participant "c-release: build 1" as B1
participant "c-release: build 2" as B2
participant "c-release: compare" as CMP
participant "c-release: publish" as P
participant "GitHub Release" as GH
C -> Q : needs quality-gate
Q --> C : green
C -> B1 : tag == v<VERSION>?
C -> B2 : tag == v<VERSION>?
B1 -> B1 : full history + tags; bootstrap kyr-build (sha256), deps.sh sysroot
B1 -> B1 : abi/layout.txt? check_abi.sh (fails the build on an unraised ABI change)
B1 -> B1 : build_deb.sh, SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH = last commit touching a build input (kyr-build >= 2.0.3)
B1 -> B1 : abi/layout.txt? check_abi.sh --exports
B2 -> B2 : the same, on another runner
B1 --> CMP : release-build-1 (debs, .buildinfo, SHA256SUMS)
B2 --> CMP : release-build-2
CMP -> CMP : diff SHA256SUMS
alt identical
  CMP --> P : ok
  P -> GH : gh release create <tag> debs SHA256SUMS buildinfo
else different
  CMP -> CMP : print buildinfo diffs, fail
end
@enduml
